{
  "slug": "jp-web-design-guardrails",
  "name": "Jp Web Design Guardrails",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Guardrails for building Japanese-ready web interfaces. Automatically enforces correct CJK typography (font stacks, line-height, kinsoku shori), Japanese form conventions (furigana fields, postal code auto-fill, Imperial era dates, confirmation screens), honorific-aware UX copy, seasonal color themes, accessibility (JIS X 8341-3), and production-ready CSS. Prevents common mistakes like using italic for emphasis, wrong name field order, and loading full CJK font files.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `jp-design` (Build Japanese-ready web interfaces with correct CJK typography, cultural UI patterns, and localization best practices).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install jp-web-design-guardrails@claude-community` from `mrslbt/jp-web-design-guardrails`.\n\nGuardrails for building Japanese-ready web interfaces with correct CJK typography, cultural UI patterns, and localization best practices.",
